WEBVTT

00:26:58.440 --> 00:27:01.885
But the feeling that I would get
when I would get those letters

00:27:01.909 --> 00:27:07.852
is, "It's so cute that you guys think
that I'm going to stop doing this

00:27:07.876 --> 00:27:10.249
just because you keep saying no."

00:27:10.273 --> 00:27:13.096
The bottom-line motivation
that I try to give people

00:27:13.120 --> 00:27:16.353
when they say, "Why should
I bother trying?

00:27:16.377 --> 00:27:19.842
Why should I bother
trying to make a thing in this world

00:27:19.866 --> 00:27:21.541
when it probably won't work?"

00:27:21.565 --> 00:27:24.489
Which -- it probably won't. You know?

00:27:24.513 --> 00:27:25.747
A lot of stuff doesn't.

00:27:25.771 --> 00:27:28.732
Most things aren't successful.
Most novels don't sell.

00:27:28.756 --> 00:27:30.088
Most movies don't get made.